    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe rule: reject creating an owner when another owner has the same `lastName` **and** `address` (compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace) \u2192 **409 Conflict**, unless the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\nThe codebase was already scaffolded for exactly this (the `DuplicateOwnerException` base explicitly names \"household\" as an intended rule, and a `HouseholdNormalizer` util and the `sharesHousehold` OpenAPI field already existed). I mirrored the existing telephone-duplicate rule:\n\n1. **`rest/advice/DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `DuplicateOwnerException` subtype carrying detail `\"An owner with the given last name and address already exists\"` and error fields `[\"lastName\", \"address\"]`. The existing generic `@ExceptionHandler(DuplicateOwnerException.class)` in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` already renders it as a uniform 409 \u2014 no advice change needed.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `rejectDuplicateHousehold(...)` to `addOwner`, right after the telephone check. It:\n   - returns early when `getSharesHousehold()` is `TRUE` (the opt-in),\n   - builds a comparison key via `HouseholdNormalizer.toComparisonKey(lastName, address)`, compares it against every existing owner's key, and throws the new exception on a match.\n\n`sharesHousehold` is a request-only directive (no `Owner` entity field), so MapStruct simply ignores it \u2014 matching the OpenAPI spec.\n\n## Test results\n- `AcceptanceTest` (the 3 household tests: reject same lastName+address, allow different address, allow with `sharesHousehold=true`): **3/3 pass**.\n- Full `./mvnw test`: **Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS** (this is the only test class in the project).",
