    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, and the body type is `OwnerFieldsDto` (not the JPA `Owner` entity).\n\n## Validations & side-effects, in order\n\n**Before the handler runs:**\n\n1. **Security filter chain** (only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`) \u2014 HTTP Basic authentication; CSRF disabled.\n2. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (enforced only when method security is enabled).\n3. **Bean Validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody` DTO** (`OwnerFieldsDto`):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with space/'/-), `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (as above, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional/nullable)\n   - Failure \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`). Note: there is **no `@NotBlank`**, so whitespace-only `address`/`city` slip through here.\n\n**Inside `addOwner`, in this exact order:**\n\n4. **`rejectBlankOwnerFields`** \u2014 firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone must be non-blank (`null`/whitespace). Failure \u2192 **400** (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException` with the offending field names). *This closes the `@NotBlank` gap above.*\n5. **`normalizeTelephone`** \u2014 normalize to E.164 (`+CC`, or assume `+61` and drop leading `0`; 8\u201315 digits), then **write the canonical value back onto the DTO** (side-effect). Invalid \u2192 **400**.\n6. **`rejectDuplicateTelephone`** \u2014 **loads all owners** (`findAllOwners()`) and compares normalized telephone keys; match \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`).\n7. **`rejectDuplicateHousehold`** \u2014 skipped if `sharesHousehold == true`; otherwise **loads all owners again** and compares a `lastName + address` comparison key; match \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`).\n8. **`normalizeEmail`** \u2014 if email present: trim, regex-check against `EMAIL_PATTERN`, lower-case, and **write back onto the DTO** (side-effect). Invalid \u2192 **400**. (Empty/null email is allowed.)\n9. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** entity (MapStruct; `id` and `pets` ignored).\n10. **Default `registrationDate`** to `LocalDate.now()` if it was null (side-effect on the entity).\n11. **`clinicService.saveOwner`** (`@Transactional`): if the owner is new and `customerCode` is null, **assign `customerCode`** = `<first 3 letters of lastName, uppercased>-<zero-padded sequence>`, where the sequence is `findAll().size() + 1` (**another full owner load**) \u2014 side-effect.\n12. **`ownerRepository.save` \u2192 `EntityManager.persist`** (INSERT). On flush, Hibernate **re-validates entity-level constraints** as a second layer: `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone, telephone `@Pattern ^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, and `@Email`. The `id` is generated via `IDENTITY`.\n13. **Build response** \u2014 map saved `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes worth calling out\n- **No entity lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist` etc.), **no custom `ConstraintValidator`s**, and **no application events** exist anywhere in this path.\n- Validation happens in **three tiers**: DTO Bean Validation (step 3), the controller's imperative guards (steps 4\u20138), and Hibernate entity constraints on flush (step 12) \u2014 with the telephone E.164 pattern effectively checked twice.\n- The duplicate checks and customer-code generation together load the full owner table **three times** per create."
  },
